the Cambridge's had arrived for their  first official visit to Ireland here on  a subtle charm offensive deployed by the  British government help smooth over  tensions caused by brexit president  Michael D Higgins and his wife were  ready to give them a warm welcome a man  committed to reconciliation he invited  William and Kate to ring the peace Bell  [Applause]  but a visit the Garden of Remembrance in  the center of Dublin was most symbolic  [Music]  as the couple bowed their heads to  remember those who lost their lives  fighting for Irish independence from  British rule it was only in 2011 that  the Queen made her first historic visit  nine years on her grandson wrote may we  never forget the lessons of history or  we continue to build a brighter future  Bobbie McDonough who was Islands  ambassador to the UK during the Queen's  visit I think a state visit or a visit  by a member of the royal family is at a  level above politics so it doesn't alter  the politics it doesn't solve the  problems that remain to be solved but it  does remind us that at a very profound  level there is a deep friendship between  Britain and Ireland in recent years we  have seen the Cambridge's picking up  more of these diplomatic elite sensitive  tours and engagements which is only to  be expected for a future king and queen  but it is likely that there are going to  be more expectations on their time as  others step back from their royal duties  Island was Harry and Megan's first tour  after they got married on Thursday Megan  is back in the UK for the first time  since they announced they want their new  life which means an unfortunate clash  with the end of the Cambridge's tour and  half the press pack heading home early  as William and Kate will continue to woo  this Irish crowd Rhiannon Mills Sky News  in Dublin
 

